# Agent Fighter — read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root first

`AGENTS.md` is the authoritative, tool-neutral working contract for this repo.
Everything below is a summary; when in doubt, open `AGENTS.md`.

Headless / recurring agents: `docs/headless-agent.md` — use `npm run fleet`
for free-tier recurring play; do not invent a second scheduler.

## The one rule

Run **`npm run verify`** before you start and before you call any change done.
It runs typecheck + the full test suite (gameplay + determinism + golden
replay + invariant guards). A red `verify` means you are NOT done. Never edit
tests or `packages/core/test/golden/hashes.json` to make it pass unless
changing them is literally the task.

## `@af/core` is a deterministic simulation — do not break it

- The sim must be **bit-identical** across browsers, Node, and re-simulation
  (rollback netcode + server verification depend on it).
- Integer fixed-point math only (24.8, `fp.ts`). **Banned in `@af/core`:**
  `Math.random`, `Date`, `performance`, DOM (`window`/`document`), timers,
  `fetch`, `process`, transcendental `Math.*` (sqrt/trig/pow/log/exp). These
  are enforced by `guards.test.ts` — they will fail `verify`.
- Every `GameState` field must be in `serialize()` and round-trip through
  `snapshot`/`restore` (state.ts). `serialize.test.ts` enforces this.
- Cosmetic effects live in client/studio, never in the sim.
- `@af/core` has ZERO dependencies. Keep it that way.

## Changing gameplay on purpose

The golden test pins current behavior. If you intend a balance/mechanic change,
run `npm run golden:bless` and commit the regenerated `hashes.json` in the same
commit. If you did NOT intend to change behavior and golden is red, you have a
regression — fix the code.

## Design

Characters are DATA (frame-data tables + cancel graphs in `characters/<id>/`
and `data.ts`/`TUNING`), never per-character code. `packages/core/src/index.ts`
is the public API contract — read it before adding core APIs; don't reach into
core internals from client/studio.
